RiceLink — Product Requirements Document
Document: Product RequirementsVersion: 1.0Status: ProposedDate: November 2026

1. Introduction
This document defines the functional and non-functional requirements for RiceLink.
RiceLink is a multi-crop agricultural supply-chain coordination platform connecting producers, aggregators, processors, storage providers, logistics operators and buyers.
The purpose of this document is to translate the product vision into requirements that the design and engineering teams can implement and test.
2. Product Goals
The platform must:
Support multiple agricultural crops.
Support multiple agricultural participant categories.
Allow producers to publish agricultural supply.
Allow buyers and processors to publish procurement requirements.
Enable users to discover relevant supply and demand.
Support coordination through enquiries.
Provide a foundation for aggregation, storage and logistics coordination.
Protect user and commercial information.
Provide administrative controls.
Support future growth without requiring major structural redesign.
3. Requirement Priorities
Requirements are classified as:
P0 — Critical: Required for the initial release.
P1 — Important: Required for the next major development phase.
P2 — Future: Planned advanced functionality.

